  "findings": [
    "No single immutable Central endpoint matrix was present in the audited branch, so native release code cannot yet consume a canonical endpoint source.",
    "The React Native Wallet hard-codes rpc.ynxweb4.com while release public facts still identify evm.ynxweb4.com as Blocked; neither source is a current Central matrix.",
    "The Wallet accepts a process-global runtime override, but this audit found no packaged immutable runtime configuration or service-discovery implementation that sets it for installed iOS/macOS releases.",
    "The macOS native application contains callback, UI, Keychain and biometric recovery boundaries but no RPC/Auth/service-discovery network client, so it cannot truthfully pass Testnet chainId or Auth flow today.",
    "Public read-only probes reached chainId 6423 from both RPC origins, but TLS establishment took 6.4-10.0 seconds and two first attempts hit a 10-second TLS timeout. This operator probe does not prove installed-app reliability.",
    "iOS ATS correctly rejects arbitrary production HTTP. Associated domains remain absent because Core has not frozen the Team ID/domain/path contract."
  ],
